Fix the build on musl

glibc's <sys/un.h> includes <string.h>, so strncpy() happens to be declared
here, while musl's <sys/un.h> does not - include <cstring> explicitly, like
src/main.cpp already does.

glibc's <sys/sysinfo.h> does not define `struct sysinfo` itself, it only pulls
in <linux/kernel.h> for the types; musl's does define it. Including
<linux/sysinfo.h> on top of that defines `struct sysinfo` twice on musl. The
kernel header is not needed, everything used here (uptime, totalram, freeram,
bufferram, mem_unit) is provided by <sys/sysinfo.h>.
--- a/src/utils/HyprlandIPC.cpp
+++ b/src/utils/HyprlandIPC.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 #include <sys/un.h>
 #include <unistd.h>

+#include <cstring>
 #include <format>

 #include <hyprutils/memory/Casts.hpp>
--- a/src/utils/SystemInfo.cpp
+++ b/src/utils/SystemInfo.cpp
@@ -17,7 +17,6 @@
 #include <pwd.h>
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
-#include <linux/sysinfo.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <glob.h>
 #include <pci/pci.h>
